#. Tag: title
#: lists.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: lists.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "lists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; has a simple and flexible list creation system. Using the same "
"interface, &kword; can create bulleted or enumerated lists of nearly any "
"depth. For easy, simple lists, &kword; offers a toolbar button for both "
"enumerated and bulleted lists."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"An enumerating style is a series of letters or numbers which proposes an "
"order or hierarchy within the list. Bullets simply mark the item as part of "
"the list and usually consist of a symbol or shape."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: lists.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "Simple lists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "To quickly create a single level list, &kword; provides two toolbar buttons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:26
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a simple enumerated list, simply select "
"<inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"enumlist.png\" format="
"\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> from the <link linkend="
"\"paragraph-toolbar\">paragraph toolbar</link>. A small menu will list "
"different enumerated list styles. Select the appropriate style and the "
"selected paragraphs are converted into a list of that style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a simple bulleted list, select "
"<inlinemediaobject><imageobject><imagedata fileref=\"bullist.png\" format="
"\"PNG\"/></imageobject></inlinemediaobject> from the <link linkend="
"\"paragraph-toolbar\">paragraph toolbar</link>. A small menu will list "
"different bulleted list styles. Select the appropriate style and the "
"selected paragraphs are converted into a bulleted list of that style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You are still able to make changes to the list styles by <link linkend="
"\"list-complex\">using the dialog</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: lists.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid "Complex lists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All complex list formatting is done through the <guilabel>Paragraph "
"Settings</guilabel> dialog. To get to the <guilabel>Paragraph Settings</"
"guilabel> dialog you can:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select <menuchoice> <guimenu>Format</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paragraph...</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Type <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Place the mouse pointer in the paragraphs that will become the list and "
"click once with the &RMB;. A small menu will appear. Select "
"<guimenuitem>Paragraph...</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A dialog will appear. To find the tab specific to lists, click once on the "
"tab labeled <guilabel>Bullets/Numbers</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: lists.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "List type"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To format the selected text as a list, select the radio button labeled "
"<guilabel>List</guilabel> from the top section of the dialog box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There is a list of five bullets types and five enumerating styles along the "
"left side of the dialog box. Select the desired list style from the list on "
"the left."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: lists.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Changing the look of the list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The text box labeled <guilabel>Prefix text:</guilabel> allows the user to "
"add text before the enumeration or bullet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The text box labeled <guilabel>Suffix text:</guilabel> allows the user to "
"add text after the enumeration or bullet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example: If <quote>Step</quote> is typed into the <guilabel>Prefix text:"
"</guilabel> box, and <quote>-</quote> is typed into the <guilabel>Suffix "
"text:</guilabel> text box, the list will look like this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: lists.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 1 - Place 1 cup of flour in a large mixing bowl."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: lists.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 2 - Add 1/4 tablespoon of yeast."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: lists.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 3 - ...."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If an enumerated list style is selected, the starting number/letter for the "
"list can be set in the spin box labeled <guilabel>Start at:</guilabel>. If "
"you have selected a bulleted list style, this box will be inactive."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: lists.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Multi-level lists"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The spin box labeled <guilabel>Depth:</guilabel> is used to add subsections "
"to your list. By selecting a depth greater than one, you are adding a "
"subsection to the list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid "Example of a multilevel enumerated list:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "An example of a multilevel bulleted list:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adjust the depth setting to determine where in the list this text occurs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By adjusting the spin box labeled <guilabel>Display levels:</guilabel> you "
"can determine if previous levels are displayed. For example, with a list "
"where <guilabel>Depth:</guilabel> is set to three and <guilabel>Display "
"levels:</guilabel> is set to one might be:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: lists.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "i. This is a step"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: lists.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "ii. This is another step"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you change the <guilabel>Display levels:</guilabel> to two, it would "
"change to:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: lists.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "A.i. This is a step"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: member
#: lists.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "A.ii. This is another step"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:133
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can always refer to the preview section of the dialog for an example of "
"how your list will look."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: lists.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "Custom Bullets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select <guilabel>Custom Bullet</guilabel> from the list of styles, "
"you can click on the button labeled <guilabel>Custom character:</guilabel> "
"to choose the letter or symbol you want for your bulleted list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: lists.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "Restart new list"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you select the checkbox labeled <guilabel>Restart numbering at this "
"paragraph</guilabel> &kword; will start numbering your list at the beginning."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: lists.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Multiple paragraphs in one list element"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each new paragraph represents a new list element. Sometimes, however, it "
"will be desireable to have multiple paragraphs on a single list element. "
"This is accomplished by inserting a New Line character instead of a "
"Paragraph Break."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: lists.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To insert a New Line, type <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>Return</"
"keycap></keycombo>."
msgstr ""

